      "answer": "Build a single, productionready promptwriting system that takes the provided technical description and rewrites it into one comprehensive, unambiguous prompt for a language model. The system must instruct the model to construct the entire target software from scratch, end to end, in complete unabridged code, while preserving the technical constraints and excluding any roleplay, filler, placeholders, simulated content, or references to the original software’s name. \n\n Core behavior\n\nThe promptwriting system must first read and absorb the full provided technical description in order, from beginning to end, and then synthesize it into a single coherent instruction set. It must explicitly require that the resulting prompt describe exactly what will be built, how it will be built, and in what sequence the implementation should proceed, so that another model can follow it without ambiguity. It must also preserve the requirement that the output be strictly technical, objective, and instructionfocused, with no polite preamble, no persona framing, and no mock or fake content. \n\n Construction rules\n\nThe rewritten prompt must demand the full software deliverable, including all files needed for a complete implementation, and it must state that the code must be productionready and unabridged. It must also preserve the instruction that, if the description refers to reimplementing an existing software, the original software name must not appear in the final prompt. The output should read like a build specification for a system being designed from zero, not like a summary of an existing product or a vague creative brief. \n\n Content handling\n\nThe system should convert the source description into one continuous prompt that covers setup, architecture, implementation steps, component behavior, file structure, and final deliverables in a single pass. It should not break the result into multiple prompts, commentary, or explanation layers. It should keep the technical content intact while reorganizing it into a clearer, more explicit sequence that a model can execute directly. \n\n Style constraints\n\nThe rewritten prompt must remain strictly technical, with objective wording and no roleplay, personalization, or filler phrases. It must avoid simplified, placeholder, dummy, simulated, or fake language, and it must explicitly require real implementation artifacts rather than illustrative standins. The wording should be direct and complete, with enough precision that the prompt can serve as a standalone specification for generating the full system. \n\n Required outcome\n\nThe final result of this promptwriting system is a single prompt that fully instructs a model to build the requested software from scratch, step by step, from initial structure to final productionready files. It should be comprehensive enough that the implementation path is obvious, the scope is fully covered, and no part of the system is left implied or underspecified.",
